Subject: HEX: Reputations and idea futures.

Some questions from Alexander Chislenko:

> Question on price setting:
> 
> If you want to sell 5 Perry positions at 400 Thorns, and I am ready to buy
> 40 at 700 Thorns, we'll have 5 changing hands... but at what price?
> 400? 700? 550?

The price will be the later of the two. This puts the onus on you to
check the current open orders before making one. In other words, if 
I offer to sell 5 Perry positions asking 400, and you then offer to buy
40 and bid 700, you are going to lose out, and I am going to make a killing.

Conversely, if you bid 100 first, and then I ask for only 50, you are going
to get the shares for only 50.

The way to avoid this, is to check the book for a stock (or at least get
a quote of last ask/bid/price) before placing an order.

